{"packet_id":"D065-01","doc_id":"D065","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"screening_restrictions","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Fair Chance in Housing Act pre-conditional-offer inquiry ban","requirement":"A housing provider may not ask about, or require an applicant to disclose, a criminal record before making a conditional offer of housing.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Any rental dwelling unit offered for rent by a housing provider; excludes a dwelling unit in an owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":true,"other":"Rental dwelling units; excludes owner-occupied premises of 4 or fewer units"},"exemptions":"Owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units; inquiry allowed into methamphetamine-manufacture convictions in federally assisted housing and lifetime sex offender registration.","penalty":"Monetary penalty up to $1,000 (no prior violation in five years), $5,000 (one prior violation), or $10,000 (two or more priors in seven years); director may order compliance measures.","effective_date":"2022-01-01","citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-55","quoted_span":"A housing provider shall not make any oral or written inquiry regarding an applicant’s criminal record prior to making a conditional offer.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D065-01","doc_id":"D065","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"application_screening_fees","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Fair Chance in Housing Act application fee disclosure","requirement":"Before accepting any application fee, a housing provider must disclose in writing whether it reviews criminal history and that the applicant may submit evidence of record inaccuracies, rehabilitation or other mitigating factors.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Any rental dwelling unit offered for rent by a housing provider that charges an application fee; excludes owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":true,"other":"Rental dwelling units; excludes owner-occupied premises of 4 or fewer units"},"exemptions":"Owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units.","penalty":"Monetary penalties up to $1,000, $5,000 or $10,000 depending on prior violations; the director may require the applicant's rental application fee be returned.","effective_date":"2022-01-01","citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-55","quoted_span":"Prior to accepting any application fee, a housing provider shall disclose in writing to the applicant: (1) Whether the eligibility criteria of the housing provider include the review and consideration of criminal history; and (2) A statement that the applicant, pursuant to subsection a. of this section, may provide evidence demonstrating inaccuracies within the applicant's criminal record or evidence of rehabilitation or other mitigating factors.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D065-01","doc_id":"D065","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"screening_restrictions","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Fair Chance in Housing Act limits on considering criminal records","requirement":"A housing provider may never consider arrests without conviction, expunged, pardoned, vacated, sealed or juvenile records, and after a conditional offer may consider only certain serious or recent convictions, after an individualized assessment.","key_value":"6-year (first degree), 4-year (second/third degree), 1-year (fourth degree) conviction lookbacks","coverage_conditions":"Any rental dwelling unit offered by a housing provider; excludes owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":true,"other":"Rental dwelling units; excludes owner-occupied premises of 4 or fewer units"},"exemptions":"Owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units.","penalty":"Monetary penalties up to $1,000, $5,000 or $10,000; director may order a conditional offer, a similar unit on the same terms, or return of the application fee.","effective_date":"2022-01-01","citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-56","quoted_span":"A housing provider shall not, either before or after the issuance of a conditional offer, evaluate an applicant based on any of the following types of criminal records: (1) arrests or charges that have not resulted in a criminal conviction; (2) expunged convictions; (3) convictions erased through executive pardon; (4) vacated and otherwise legally nullified convictions;","interaction":null,"confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D065-01","doc_id":"D065","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"screening_restrictions","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Fair Chance in Housing Act advertisement restriction","requirement":"A housing provider may not publish housing advertisements stating that it will not consider any applicant who has been arrested or convicted of a crime or offense.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Housing advertisements by a housing provider for rental dwelling units; excludes owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":true,"other":"Rental dwelling units; excludes owner-occupied premises of 4 or fewer units"},"exemptions":"Advertisements about methamphetamine-manufacture convictions in federally assisted housing and lifetime sex offender registration.","penalty":"Monetary penalties up to $1,000, $5,000 or $10,000.","effective_date":"2022-01-01","citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-58","quoted_span":"A housing provider shall not knowingly or purposefully publish, or cause to be published, any housing advertisement that explicitly provides that the housing provider will not consider any applicant who has been arrested or convicted of one or more crimes or offenses,","interaction":null,"confidence":0.9,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D065-01","doc_id":"D065","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Eviction after successful appeal of director's Fair Chance order","requirement":"If a housing provider wins an appeal overturning the director's order, that determination is grounds to evict a former applicant who occupies the unit because of the order, after at least 45 days' notice.","key_value":"45 days' notice","coverage_conditions":"A former applicant residing in a rental dwelling unit owned by the housing provider as the result of a director's order later overturned on appeal.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"Rental dwelling unit occupied under a director's order later overturned"},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":"2022-01-01","citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-63","quoted_span":"a determination that the housing provider did not violate the provisions of this act as evidenced by such successful appeal shall be grounds for the housing provider to evict the former applicant if that person resides in a rental dwelling unit owned by the housing provider as the result of the director’s order, so long as the housing provider provides the applicant with at least 45 days’ notice prior to the eviction;","interaction":"Applies notwithstanding the Anti-Eviction Act, P.L.1974, c.49 (C.2A:18-61.1 et seq.).","confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
